# Pawnstar opening set, for SPRT matches and self-play data generation.
#
# Generated by tools/make_openings.sh from pawnstar.book, which is the opening book of TSCP
# (Tom Kerrigan's Simple Chess Program, https://github.com/terredeciels/TSCP) and is in the
# PUBLIC DOMAIN - so this set carries no licence restriction of its own and no third party's
# data. Every book line was replayed from the start position, and each position it reached
# between ply 4 and ply 24 was kept when the engine's static NNUE evaluation of it was
# within 125 centipawns of its evaluation of the start position (158 cp, White's
# perspective); then duplicates were removed. The book's 385 lines overlap heavily and hold only
# about 420 distinct positions in this window, so this is near the ceiling of the source: an SPRT
# with more rounds than there are openings here replays some of them.
#
# One position per line, as the first four FEN fields. Lines beginning with '#' are comments:
# tools/gen_data.cpp skips them, and tools/run_sprt.sh strips them before handing the file to
# fastchess, whose EPD reader does not.
